<newsitem itemid="47707" id="root" date="1996-09-11" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Coats Viyella H1 beats forecasts.</title>
<headline>Coats Viyella H1 beats forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		3.6		    vs 6.4</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.70		   vs 3.70</p>
<p> Pretax		     47.0		   vs 70.8</p>
<p> Turnover		   1,160		  vs 1,199</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits were in a range of 39.0 to 43.2 million stg. The result included a restructuring charge of 17.2 million stg. The company expects underlying second half results to show a &quot;worthwhile improvement&quot; from a year earlier.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 78.0		   vs 87.9</p>
<p> Exceptional		17.2 loss	    vs 2.8 loss</p>
<p> Interest paid	    19.5		   vs 16.4</p>
<p> Tax			  17.2		   vs 21.2</p>
<p> Net taxed		  29.8		   vs 49.6</p>
<p> Attributable	     27.9		   vs 46.3</p>
<p> Pay date		   Dec 24</p>
<p>Div registration date  Nov 26</p>
<p>NOTE- Coats Viyella is paying a Foreign Income Dividend (FID) of 4.625 pence per share, unchanged from a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
